<title>SINGAPORE: Indonesia details 3.1 mln bbl June LSWR allocation.</title>
<headline>Indonesia details 3.1 mln bbl June LSWR allocation.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's state oil company Pertamina has announced the loading schedule for its 3.1 million barrels of low sulphur waxy residue for June lifting, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Traders expected the market to firm slightly in June amid slightly tighter supplies and Korean Electric Power Company (KEPCO) tender to buy half a million barrels of LSWR for delivery in July.</p>
<p>Although KEPCO's tender will be for July delivery, traders said the tender will helped boost sentiment after a recent lull in the market.  </p>
<p>    SUB TOTAL:     400</p>
<p>LOADING FROM BALIKPAPAN (KALIMANTAN, BORNEO)</p>
<p>     16-18	   200	 Pacific Petroleum</p>
<p>     19-21	   200	 Pacific Petroleum</p>
<p>     25-27	   100	 Pacific Petroleum</p>
<p>     25-27	   100	 Indoil</p>
<p>     28-30	   150	 Itochu</p>
<p>     28-30	    50	 Indoil</p>
<p>    SUB TOTAL:     800</p>
<p>    TOTAL	  3,100</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3571)</p>
